WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.992
A traceability matrix is a practical
teaching tool for connecting needs to

2
00:00:05.142 --> 00:00:06.224
evidence.

3
00:00:06.374 --> 00:00:10.598
Each row links a requirement to its design
response, relevant risk

4
00:00:10.748 --> 00:00:13.649
control, verification activity and result.

5
00:00:13.799 --> 00:00:18.301
A check mark is not enough if the
underlying record cannot be located.

6
00:00:18.451 --> 00:00:22.952
For our vessel, the product-contact-
material requirement links to a design

7
00:00:23.102 --> 00:00:27.667
specification, installed material records
and the review that confirms

8
00:00:27.817 --> 00:00:29.972
suitability for the intended use.

9
00:00:30.722 --> 00:00:32.834
The three cards show different states.

10
00:00:32.984 --> 00:00:36.376
A planned test has an approved method but
no result.

11
00:00:36.526 --> 00:00:40.857
An executed test has observations, which
may include a failure.

12
00:00:41.007 --> 00:00:46.084
An accepted result has been evaluated
against the applicable criteria with

13
00:00:46.234 --> 00:00:48.623
deviations addressed appropriately.

14
00:00:48.773 --> 00:00:52.699
Keeping these states separate prevents a
dashboard from showing green

15
00:00:52.849 --> 00:00:55.302
simply because someone uploaded a file.

16
00:00:55.452 --> 00:00:59.548
The evidence must answer the requirement,
not merely share its title.

17
00:01:00.298 --> 00:01:04.074
A supplier may provide useful testing and
design records.

18
00:01:04.224 --> 00:01:07.403
Review whether they apply to the purchased
configuration,

19
00:01:07.553 --> 00:01:10.923
use appropriate methods and preserve
reliable data.

20
00:01:11.073 --> 00:01:15.895
Transport, installation or configuration
changes can affect whether a

21
00:01:16.045 --> 00:01:17.858
result remains applicable.

22
00:01:18.008 --> 00:01:23.449
Our example is a factory test of an alarm
that depends on a site-installed sensor.

23
00:01:23.599 --> 00:01:27.844
The team must assess what needs
verification after installation.

24
00:01:27.994 --> 00:01:32.026
A supplier signature does not settle that
question automatically.

25
00:01:32.776 --> 00:01:36.147
In the activity, construct five
traceability rows.

26
00:01:36.297 --> 00:01:40.627
Mark the status honestly and identify the
next action for each gap.

27
00:01:40.777 --> 00:01:44.660
A requirement with no test may need a new
verification method.

28
00:01:44.810 --> 00:01:51.373
A test with no requirement may reveal an
undocumented need or unnecessary work.

29
00:01:51.523 --> 00:01:55.448
Traceability should support technical
thinking in both directions.

30
00:01:55.598 --> 00:01:58.137
It is a means of exposing missing
evidence,

31
00:01:58.287 --> 00:02:02.084
not a substitute for judging whether that
evidence is adequate.
